-- title:
--   Integral closedness of the localised modular subring
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field, $A$ a valuation subring of $L$, $k$ a field and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism from the underlying subring of $A$; let $N \ge 1$ and let `data` be modular polynomial data for $N$, that is a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(N)$ with $\Phi(j(q), j(q^N)) = 0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, where $\psi(N) = \sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$. Write $O$ for `modularLocalized N A.toSubring red`, the subring of $L((q))$ consisting of those $f$ with $f s = r$ for some $r, s$ in the subring generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with $j(q)$ and $j(q^N)$, with $s$ outside the prime ideal `redKer` cut out by $\mathrm{red}$; thus $O$ is the localisation of that subring at `redKer`, realised inside $L((q))$. Assume the degree hypothesis that over the residue field $k$ the extension $k(j(q), j(q^N))$ of $k(j(q))$, both taken inside $k((q))$, has relative degree exactly $\psi(N)$. Then for every $x \in L((q))$ lying in the subfield $L(j(q), j(q^N))$ which satisfies a monic polynomial equation $p(x) = 0$ with coefficients in $O$ (read in $L((q))$ through the inclusion of $O$), one has $x \in O$.
--
--   This is the integral closedness of the localised modular presentation ring inside the two-generator modular function field over $L$, conditional on the degree of the special fibre being the generic degree $\psi(N)$. It feeds the construction of the characteristic-$p$ model of $X_0(N)$, being used by the lemmas producing fibre models and charts at the cusps and the factorisation statements for elements killed by the reduction homomorphism.
